@MT I'm thinking more about IPR. What if the idea from anonymous-address gets in the RFC and then once it's deployed someone else with a real name declares they have a preexisting patent on it and starts suing the implementers

Right.  The W3C manages this by distinguishing between non-substantive and substantive contributions.

